Stephan Leake asks :

>Is there any way to make my (great, wonderful, fun, reliable) DECwindows/DECNET
>platform (a VAXstation 3100), into a TCP X client, so I can run X applications
>on other machines, with the display on my machine? Obviously, they are running  
>Unix, in this particular case, IBM AIX. We have Multinet for TCP access.

Yes, but you need to install TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS (aka UCX), or
whatever it is called now. This should allow any TCP connects to your VAxstation,
(don't forget your security). Install the TCP/IP transport in DECwindows as 
well. Look in SYS$STARTUP:DECW$PRIVATE_SERVER_SETUP.TEMPLATE (?) and this will
tell you how to do this.

Simon
Digital Newbury, UK

